  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"we should be able to drag and drop a STEP file into the view and get it loaded as model.\"\n\nWhat is missing: a model is loaded only through the Model > Open dialog. Dropping a file from the file manager onto the window does nothing.\n\nWanted: dropping a STEP file (`.step`, `.stp`) on the viewport loads it as the model, through the same undoable import command the Model dialog uses (no second import path). The other formats the importer already reads (STL and any others the Model dialog offers) are taken the same way. While a file is dragged over the window, the viewport shows a plain \"Drop to load model\" hint.\n\nRules:\n- One command, the existing one: undo removes the dropped model exactly as it does after the dialog.\n- A file the importer cannot read, an unsupported extension, or several files dropped at once: a clear message naming the file and the reason; never a crash or a half-loaded model (Prime Directive: corrupt STEP/STL gives a clean error).\n- If the project already has a model, the drop behaves as the Model dialog does in that case (the same question or the same refusal), not a silent replace.\n- Browser build: a drop there hands over bytes, not a path; it follows the browser file work of issue 1431 and may land after it. The desktop build is the scope here.\n\nDone means: a STEP file dropped on the viewport appears as the model and Ctrl+Z removes it; a corrupt file and an unsupported file each show a named message and leave the project unchanged; the drop goes through the import command (pinned by a ui test that feeds a dropped-file event through the test harness); the hint is covered by the structural test.\n",
